  /**
   * Simulate a sandbox session's status
   *
   * <p>Force a terminal status on a sandbox session after the fact, from your backend, without running the flow. Sandbox applications only: a live session returns <code>404</code>. Works for User Verification (KYC) and Business Verification (KYB) sessions.
   *
   * <p>Set <code>new_status</code>, or let <code>scenario</code> or <code>risk</code> supply it. <code>risk</code> (or the first risk the scenario's magic values carry) adds that warning to the session. The change is recorded in the session's activity.
   *
   * <p><code>send_webhooks</code> (default <code>true</code>) sends exactly the webhooks a real status change sends. With <code>false</code> the status still changes and the console still updates live, but no webhook is logged or sent, the missed-webhook recovery never re-sends that decision, and the next status change sends webhooks as usual. The response echoes the value applied.
   *
   * <p>Requires the <code>write:sessions</code> privilege; a scoped API key needs write access to sessions. An unknown <code>session_id</code> returns <code>404</code> and another application's session returns <code>403</code>, both before the body is read; a live session returns <code>404</code> only after the body is validated. To simulate from the hosted flow with the session's own token, use <code>POST /v3/session/{sessionId}/sandbox/simulate/</code>. See [Sandbox &amp; Test Data](/integration/sandbox-testing) for the scenario catalog.
   *
   * <p>{@code POST /v3/session/{sessionId}/simulate/}
   *
   * @param sessionId UUID of the sandbox verification session. Accepts both user (KYC) and business (KYB) session IDs.
   * @param params the request parameters
   * @param options per-request options that override the client options
   * @return the response body
   */
  public SandboxSimulateResponse simulate(String sessionId, SandboxSimulateRequest params, RequestOptions options) {
    return client.execute(simulateRequest(sessionId, params), options, SIMULATE_RESPONSE).data();
  }

